# Merging an exposure bracket into one scene-linear image.
#
# Drop your bracket on one palette row -- hold ALT while dropping to make them
# a group in one go -- then right-click the group and "Sort by filename" so the
# order is what you expect.
#
# merge_hdr reads each frame's shutter, aperture and ISO from its EXIF and
# divides them out, so every frame contributes the same radiance where it is
# well exposed. The result carries real headroom: values well above 1.0 where
# the scene was brighter than any single frame could hold.
#
# Watch the status line after a run -- it reports how many stops the bracket
# spanned, and warns if a frame carried no exposure metadata.

frames = image("bracket")
merged = merge_hdr(frames)

# The merge is scene-linear, so exposure here means what it means on a raw:
# a stop is a stop. Pull the highlights down to see what the bracket captured
# above what one frame could hold.
final = basic_adjust(merged, auto_exposure = 1)

display(merged, "linear")
display(final,  "developed")
